 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How did one sultan grow the empire by seventy percent in eight years?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Selim the First did it. He took eastern Anatolia, Syria, Egypt, and the holy cities of Arabia."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How big was the empire when he took over?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1512",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It held the Balkans and most of Anatolia. To the east was a new power in Iran: the Safavids. To the south, the Mamluks of Egypt."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In 1512, Selim pushed his own father off the throne. The Turks call him Yavuz: the stern one.",
   "scene": "selim",
   "date": "1512",
   "place": "Istanbul",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.38,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "say": "In 1512, Selim pushed his own father off the throne. The Turks call him Yavooz: the stern one."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Who were the Safavids?",
   "scene": "ismail",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.42,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "A new dynasty led by Shah Ismail. Many Turkmen in eastern Anatolia followed him, and Selim saw that as a threat."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In August 1514, the two armies met at Chaldiran, in today's northwest Iran.",
   "scene": "chaldiranmap",
   "date": "August 1514",
   "place": "Chaldiran"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The Ottomans had cannons and muskets behind a wall of carts. The Safavids had no cannons at all.",
   "scene": "guns"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Ismail was wounded and barely escaped.",
   "scene": "chaldiranp",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.45,
     0.35,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Did Selim keep Iran?",
   "scene": "chaldiran",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.6,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not exactly. He took the Safavid capital, Tabriz, but his soldiers would not stay, so he pulled back. He kept eastern Anatolia instead."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And after that?",
   "scene": "mamlukmap",
   "date": "1516",
   "place": "Syria"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He turned south, against the Mamluks. In August 1516, at Marj Dabiq near Aleppo, the Mamluk sultan died on the battlefield."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Five months later, Selim defeated the last Mamluk sultan outside Cairo, and took the city."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Cairo had been the Mamluk capital for over two hundred and fifty years.",
   "scene": "cairo",
   "date": "1517",
   "place": "Cairo",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.6,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And Mecca?",
   "scene": "marj",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.6,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The ruler of Mecca accepted Ottoman rule. Selim took the title Servant of the Two Holy Cities."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So how much bigger was the empire?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1520",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "About seventy percent bigger, in just eight years. Selim died in 1520."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: his son, Suleiman the Magnificent. Like the video and follow History Sketches.",
   "scene": "selimlate",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: Suleiman the Magnificent",
